# Line endings are load-bearing in this subtree, not cosmetic.
#
# eval/frozen.sha256 hashes the WORKING-TREE BYTES of the frozen oracle/harness/tests, so a
# checkout that lands CRLF fails verify_frozen_manifest() and no scored run can start — which is
# exactly what happened when this campaign was first cloned onto Windows with core.autocrlf=true
# (all four frozen files reported MODIFIED although their content was byte-for-byte correct once
# normalized). See autoresearch/PORTING.md.
#
# eol=lf pins the checkout to LF on every platform, so the manifest matches everywhere; text=auto
# keeps whatever a Windows tool writes with CRLF (dashboard.py, log.md edits) normalized in the
# index instead of showing up as a whole-file diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary payloads: never touch these bytes.
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.gz binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.ipynb -text
